{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773097091,"nonce":"kRenG361zyWJeZxHfdpVVRP2eE8=","title":"GraphCanvas: graph zoom/layout resets on filter change (alpha restart disrupts node positions)","message":"When the time-range or status filter changes in the GraphView, the simulation calls sim.alpha(0.4).restart(). Even though existing node x/y positions are preserved via Object.assign(prev, node), alpha=0.4 gives the simulation significant energy — forces (charge, link, center) push nodes around and the layout scrambles. The zoom TRANSFORM itself is preserved, but nodes scatter, which the user perceives as zoom reset.\n\nAttempt 1 (failed — 2026-03-09): Added zoomRef to store D3 zoom behavior. This was the wrong fix — it addresses zoom transform reset (which was not happening) rather than the simulation restart problem.\n\nReal fix needed: When updating nodes/edges due to filter change, avoid high-alpha restart if the user has manually panned/zoomed the viewport. Options:\n1. Use a much lower alpha on data update (e.g., 0.05 or even 0) so forces minimally perturb existing positions\n2. Dont","files":null}]}